xnu 0436: read back the BHI doorbell and the WLAN SMMU fault state

The 4 KiB and 512 KiB loads now fail cleanly with BHI_STATUS still 0x0 after
ten seconds, and no line says whether the device fetched the image. Add one
diagnostic read after the wait: image address, size, doorbell and status, plus
the context SCTLR/FSR/FAR/FSYNR0, the global FSR and both S2CR routes.

A translation fault with a matching FAR proves the BHI read reached the SMMU
and the page table is wrong; a clean FSR with a stuck doorbell proves the
device never started the transfer. The register offsets match mainline MHI
(BHI_IMGADDR 0x08/0x0c, IMGSIZE 0x10, IMGTXDB 0x18, STATUS 0x2c).

